# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file is committed FIRST, before any source arrives. That is deliberate.
#
# On a prior engagement customer records reached a repository and needed a git
# history rewrite to remove. The window in which that happens is between
# `git init` and these rules landing — so it is closed first.
#
# Verify, do not assume:   git check-ignore -v <path>
# Re-verify after ANY bulk file copy — a .gitignore can be silently overwritten
# and `git status` will not tell you.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── CUSTOMER DATA — never, under any circumstances ───────────────────────────
exports/
attached_assets/
reports/
uploads/
screenshots/
.canvas/
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.sql
*.dump
*.vcf

# ── CREDENTIALS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*credentials*
*service-account*

# ── RAW SESSION TRANSCRIPTS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These contain secrets in plain text, plus server addresses and findings about
# customer records. A redacted docs/SESSION-CHAT.md is the safe derivative.
*.jsonl
session-transcript*

# ── IMAGES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Screenshots have contained customer names, account balances and identity
# documents. Blanket-blocked; add a narrow exception if a repo genuinely needs
# one, and say why in the commit.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.pdf

# ── SOURCE IMAGE ASSETS — narrow exceptions to the blanket block above ──────
# The blanket image block exists because screenshots have carried customer names,
# balances and identity documents. These directories are different: they are the
# application's own brand and product artwork, imported by the source and already
# served publicly on the live site. Every file was opened and checked before this
# exception was added.
#
# Blocking them broke the build — Vite failed with 'Failed to resolve import' and
# the preview would not render at all.
#
# Keep these narrow. Never negate a whole tree, and never add one without looking
# at the files first. Build output under dist/ stays excluded.

!artifacts/affiliate-dashboard/public/**

# ── BUILD OUTPUT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
build/
out/
.next/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── DEPENDENCIES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.venv/
__pycache__/

# ── REPLIT WORKSPACE STATE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Carried over from the export's own .gitignore. `.local/` is the pnpm
# content-addressable store — 190 MB of the 209 MB export. Never commit it.
.cache/
.local/
tmp/
out-tsc/
.expo/
.expo-shared/

# ── EDITOR / OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ── LOCAL AI SESSION STATE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .claude/rules/ and .claude/launch.json ARE committed — they must travel with
# the repo, because a cloud session clones only this repository.
.claude/settings.local.json

# KYC uploads (customer identity documents) — never commit
.data/
